 description JHYY (机会翼游) - a self-hosted, statically typed, expression-oriented systems language. The compiler is written in itself and reproduces itself byte-for-byte to a fixed point. The backend is a self-written amd64 emitter - no QBE, no LLVM, no GC, no managed runtime.
 issues 0

example
 extern fn puts(s: *u8) -> i32;

 fn main_jhyy() -> i32 {
     puts("Hello, world!");
     0
 }

 description Hello world. The hosted entry point of a JHYY program is main_jhyy rather than main, and C library functions are reached through extern fn declarations on the C ABI.
 fileExtensions jhyy
 website https://github.com/JiHuiYiYou/JiHuiYiYou-compiler
 gitRepo https://github.com/JiHuiYiYou/JiHuiYiYou-compiler
example
 type Point = struct { x: i32, y: i32 }

 fn dist_sq(a: Point, b: Point) -> i32 {
     let dx = a.x - b.x;
     let dy = a.y - b.y;
     dx * dx + dy * dy
 }

 fn classify(n: i32) -> *u8 {
     match n {
         0       => "zero",
         1..10   => "single digit",
         10 | 20 => "round number",
         _       => "other",
     }
 }

